    <!--
      The statement. A statement to agree with, never a question about a diagnosis.
      TODO(clinician): review the quote, the body and both answers before release.
      The design's body ends "and the answer stays on this phone", which is not true: the answer
      is saved with the rest of the settings, and settings sync to the person's account. The body
      says what a yes does: it keeps Full numbers off the starting list, the fasting timer off
      and watch activity out of the range (Settings.exerciseInRange, Fasts).
    -->
    <string name="onboarding_q_statement">Does this sound like you?</string>
    <string name="onboarding_statement_quote">“Numbers or tracking have been hard for me before.”</string>
    <string name="onboarding_statement_body">If you say yes, you get gentler starting points, and fasting and exercise adjustments stay off. We don't ask why.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_statement_yes">Yes, that's me</string>
    <string name="onboarding_statement_no">Not really</string>
